"""Agent factory for the ``$node_id`` step (template: websearch).

**Re-probed against the pinned 2.43.0 wheel and found to differ from
PLAN.md fact 9** (see GROUP2_PLAN.md's final report for the full
write-up): fact 9 says ``toolsets=[WebSearchTool(...)]`` is the correct
call site. Constructing an ``Agent`` that way DOES succeed (fact 9's
construction-time claim holds), but calling ``.run()`` on it raises
``TypeError: 'WebSearchTool' object is not callable`` -- `toolsets=`
expects toolset objects/factories, and ``WebSearchTool`` is not one (it
is an ``AbstractNativeTool``, unrelated to ``AbstractToolset``).

The verified-working construction is ``capabilities=[NativeTool(...)]``
from ``pydantic_ai.capabilities`` (confirmed against the installed
2.43.0 wheel: ``Agent(model, capabilities=[NativeTool(WebSearchTool())])``
constructs AND runs). ``builtin_tools=`` still does not exist (fact 9
half still holds) and plain ``tools=[WebSearchTool()]`` still raises
``AttributeError`` (fact 9's other half also still holds) -- only the
*correct* call site changed from what PLAN.md documented.
"""

